---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CodeWindow from '../components/CodeWindow.astro';

const agents = ['Claude Code', 'Codex', 'OpenCode', 'Pi'];
---

<Base>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="hero-grid border-b border-neutral-200">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl items-center gap-12 px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:py-28">
      <div>
        <p class="font-mono text-sm text-neutral-500">
          <span class="text-emerald-600">$</span> recall <span class="text-neutral-300">·</span> local
          memory for coding agents
        </p>
        <h1
          class="mt-5 text-4xl font-bold leading-[1.05] tracking-tight text-neutral-900 sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl"
        >
          Never lose the context of a coding session again.
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-neutral-600">
          Recall indexes your Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, and Pi sessions into
          a local SQLite knowledge base. Search, resume, and build on everything
          you have already done — nothing leaves your machine.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
          <a
            href="/docs/usage"
            class="rounded-lg bg-neutral-900 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-white transition-colors hover:bg-neutral-700"
          >
            Install in Pi
          </a>
          <a
            href="/docs"
            class="rounded-lg border border-neutral-300 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-neutral-900 transition-colors hover:bg-neutral-50"
          >
            Read the docs
          </a>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/viggy28/recall"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-neutral-500 hover:text-neutral-900"
          >
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M12 .5C5.65.5.5 5.65.5 12c0 5.08 3.29 9.39 7.86 10.91.58.11.79-.25.79-.55v-2.15c-3.2.7-3.87-1.36-3.87-1.36-.52-1.33-1.28-1.69-1.28-1.69-1.04-.71.08-.7.08-.7 1.15.08 1.76 1.18 1.76 1.18 1.03 1.76 2.69 1.25 3.35.96.1-.75.4-1.25.72-1.54-2.55-.29-5.23-1.28-5.23-5.68 0-1.26.45-2.29 1.18-3.09-.12-.29-.51-1.46.11-3.05 0 0 .96-.31 3.15 1.18a10.9 10.9 0 0 1 5.74 0c2.19-1.49 3.15-1.18 3.15-1.18.62 1.59.23 2.76.11 3.05.74.8 1.18 1.83 1.18 3.09 0 4.41-2.69 5.38-5.25 5.67.41.35.78 1.05.78 2.12v3.14c0 .3.21.66.8.55A10.51 10.51 0 0 0 23.5 12C23.5 5.65 18.35.5 12 .5Z" />
            </svg>
            Star on GitHub
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="lg:pl-4">
        <CodeWindow title="recall">
          <div class="space-y-1.5">
            <p>
              <span class="text-emerald-400">$</span>{' '}
              <span class="text-neutral-100">recall index</span>
            </p>
            <p>
              <span class="text-emerald-400">$</span>{' '}
              <span class="text-neutral-100">recall search</span>{' '}
              <span class="text-accent-300">"why did we change the retry logic"</span>
            </p>
            <p class="pt-1 text-neutral-500">▸ pi · recall · 2 weeks ago</p>
            <p class="text-neutral-300">
              "Switched retries to exponential backoff because the upstream API
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-300">
              rate-limits bursts and three retries were burning the budget."
            </p>
            <p class="pt-2 text-neutral-500">▸ opencode · api-client · 1 month ago</p>
            <p class="text-neutral-300">
              "Timeout defaults are too aggressive for large payloads —"
            </p>
          </div>
        </CodeWindow>
        <p class="mt-4 text-center font-mono text-xs text-neutral-400">
          fuzzy · regex · local semantic search
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why -->
  <section class="border-b border-neutral-200 bg-neutral-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:py-24">
      <div class="max-w-2xl">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-neutral-400">
          Why Recall
        </p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 sm:text-4xl">
          Your agents remember the work. You don't.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-neutral-600">
          Coding agents produce hundreds of sessions. The decisions live in
          transcripts you'll never reopen.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white p-7">
          <p class="font-mono text-sm font-medium text-accent-600">01</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900">
            You've already solved this.
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-600">
            A bug you fixed months ago just came back. The fix — and the{" "}
            <em>why</em> behind it — is buried in a transcript you'll never
            reopen. Recall makes it one search away.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white p-7">
          <p class="font-mono text-sm font-medium text-accent-600">02</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900">
            Every session starts cold.
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-600">
            The migration plan, the naming decisions, the workarounds — all
            scattered across tools and gone the moment a session ends. Recall
            keeps the context and lets you attach it to the next one.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white p-7">
          <p class="font-mono text-sm font-medium text-accent-600">03</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900">
            Your history is yours.
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-600">
            Sessions are full of private decisions and half-formed ideas. They
            belong on your machine, not in someone else's cloud. Recall is
            local by default.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What it does -->
  <section class="border-b border-neutral-200">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:py-24">
      <div class="max-w-2xl">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-neutral-400">
          What Recall does
        </p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 sm:text-4xl">
          A searchable memory, in plain Markdown and SQLite.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 bg-neutral-200 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        <!-- Search -->
        <div class="bg-white p-7">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-neutral-900" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7" />
            <path d="m20 20-3.5-3.5" />
          </svg>
          <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-semibold text-neutral-900">Search everything</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-600">
            Fuzzy, regex, or optional local semantic search across all your
            sessions — filter by source, project, role, or date. Find the exact
            message where you solved it.
          </p>
        </div>
        <!-- Browse -->
        <div class="bg-white p-7">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-neutral-900" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" />
            <path d="M12 7v5l3 3" />
          </svg>
          <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-semibold text-neutral-900">Browse &amp; resume</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-600">
            See recent conversations and jump back into supported sessions
            without digging through folders.
          </p>
        </div>
        <!-- Context banks -->
        <div class="bg-white p-7">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-neutral-900" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M6 3h9l3 3v15H6z" />
            <path d="M9 3v3h6" />
            <path d="M9 12h6M9 16h6" />
          </svg>
          <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-semibold text-neutral-900">Context banks</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-600">
            Turn hard-won context into plain Markdown you can review, revise,
            undo, export, and attach to future sessions.
          </p>
        </div>
        <!-- Knowledge graphs -->
        <div class="bg-white p-7">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-neutral-900" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="6" cy="6" r="2.5" />
            <circle cx="18" cy="8" r="2.5" />
            <circle cx="10" cy="18" r="2.5" />
            <path d="M8 7.5 15.5 8M7.5 8l1.5 7.5M17 10.5 12 16" />
          </svg>
          <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-semibold text-neutral-900">Knowledge graphs</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-600">
            Extract entities and relationships from your sessions as JSON or
            DOT. See how the pieces of your work connect.
          </p>
        </div>
        <!-- Local -->
        <div class="bg-white p-7">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-neutral-900" aria-hidden="true">
            <rect x="4" y="10" width="16" height="10" rx="2" />
            <path d="M8 10V7a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3" />
          </svg>
          <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-semibold text-neutral-900">Local by default</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-600">
            SQLite FTS5 under the hood. Core indexing and search use only the
            Python standard library — nothing is uploaded.
          </p>
        </div>
        <!-- CLI / extension -->
        <div class="bg-white p-7">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-neutral-900" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M4 17 10 11 4 5" />
            <path d="M12 19h8" />
          </svg>
          <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-semibold text-neutral-900">CLI or extension</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-600">
            A standalone Python CLI, or a native Pi extension with{" "}
            <code class="font-mono text-[0.85em]">/recall</code>,{" "}
            <code class="font-mono text-[0.85em]">recall_search</code>, and{" "}
            <code class="font-mono text-[0.85em]">recall_context</code>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Works where you work -->
  <section class="border-b border-neutral-200 bg-neutral-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6">
      <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-6 text-center">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-neutral-400">
          Works where you work
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3">
          {agents.map((agent) => (
            <span class="rounded-full border border-neutral-300 bg-white px-4 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-neutral-700">
              {agent}
            </span>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Install -->
  <section id="install" class="border-b border-neutral-200">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:py-24">
      <div class="max-w-2xl">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-neutral-400">
          Install
        </p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 sm:text-4xl">
          Up and running in a minute.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 p-7">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="rounded bg-neutral-900 px-2 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs font-medium text-white">
              Pi
            </span>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900">Pi extension</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-600">
            Adds the <code class="font-mono text-[0.85em]">/recall</code>{' '}
            dashboard plus the <code class="font-mono text-[0.85em]">recall_search</code>{' '}
            and <code class="font-mono text-[0.85em]">recall_context</code> tools.
            Ask naturally, right where you work.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-5 rounded-lg bg-neutral-950 p-4 font-mono text-sm text-neutral-100">
            <p><span class="text-emerald-400">$</span> pi install npm:recall-pi</p>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-neutral-500">
            <em>"Search my sessions for the retry backoff change."</em>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 p-7">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="rounded bg-neutral-900 px-2 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs font-medium text-white">
              CLI
            </span>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900">Standalone CLI</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-600">
            Core search has no required third-party dependencies. Install the{" "}
            <code class="font-mono text-[0.85em]">recall</code> command for the
            full experience.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-5 space-y-1 rounded-lg bg-neutral-950 p-4 font-mono text-sm text-neutral-100">
            <p><span class="text-emerald-400">$</span> python3 recall.py index</p>
            <p><span class="text-emerald-400">$</span> python3 recall.py search <span class="text-accent-300">"deadlock investigation"</span></p>
            <p><span class="text-emerald-400">$</span> python3 recall.py recent</p>
          </div>
          <a href="/docs/usage" class="mt-4 inline-block text-sm font-medium text-accent-600 hover:text-accent-700">
            Full usage guide →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Demo -->
  <section class="border-b border-neutral-200 bg-neutral-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:py-24">
      <div class="max-w-2xl">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-neutral-400">
          See it in action
        </p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 sm:text-4xl">
          Search, review, and reuse — from the terminal.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white">
          <img
            src="/images/recall-demo.gif"
            alt="Animated walkthrough of Recall search, Pi tools, and context banks"
            class="w-full"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <div class="border-t border-neutral-200 px-5 py-4">
            <p class="text-sm font-medium text-neutral-900">Search &amp; session tools</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-neutral-500">
              Fuzzy, regex, and semantic search over every indexed session.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white">
          <img
            src="/images/context-review.svg"
            alt="Recall reviewing an update to a context bank with Apply, Revise, and Cancel controls"
            class="w-full"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <div class="border-t border-neutral-200 px-5 py-4">
            <p class="text-sm font-medium text-neutral-900">Context bank review</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-neutral-500">
              Every update is reviewed before it overwrites saved context.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Local / privacy band -->
  <section class="border-b border-neutral-200 bg-neutral-900">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <p class="font-mono text-sm text-emerald-400"># local by default</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-4xl">
          Yours, on your machine.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-neutral-300">
          Recall reads local transcripts and writes its index to{" "}
          <code class="font-mono text-sm text-neutral-200">~/.recall/recall.db</code>.
          Core indexing and search use only the Python standard library and
          never send your conversations anywhere. Optional semantic search
          downloads and runs an embedding model locally.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-white/10 p-5">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-white">Nothing uploaded</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-400">
            Your transcripts stay on disk. The index is local SQLite.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-white/10 p-5">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-white">Stdlib-only core</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-400">
            Indexing and search need no third-party packages at all.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-white/10 p-5">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-white">Local embeddings</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-400">
            Optional semantic search runs the model on your machine.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Docs / blog CTA -->
  <section class="border-b border-neutral-200">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-6 px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <a
        href="/docs"
        class="group rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 p-7 transition-colors hover:border-neutral-400"
      >
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900">Read the docs</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-neutral-600">
          Installation, search, context banks, architecture, and releases.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-accent-600 group-hover:text-accent-700">
          Browse documentation →
        </p>
      </a>
      <a
        href="/blog"
        class="group rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 p-7 transition-colors hover:border-neutral-400"
      >
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900">Read the blog</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-neutral-600">
          How Recall is built, and why it works the way it does.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-accent-600 group-hover:text-accent-700">
          Browse the blog →
        </p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
